From 744b386e9e8dc1284504c4beb6897baa220f5889 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:06:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GUIInfo, video settings: the Dolby Vision state for any skin,
 and its output chosen from a list

The player information of Hades shows how a Dolby Vision video goes out and
what the display is sent, and the video settings of the player let the user
choose another output for that video ("Dolby Vision output (this video)").
Neither could be reached from another skin's own controls: the values are
published only as properties of the Home window, under names of Hades' pages,
and the choice only from the settings list.

Labels in Kodi's Player.Process() provider, documented with the others:
- videooutputhdrtype: what the display is sent: dolbyvision, hdr10plus, hdr10,
  hlg or sdr (the name and the values are those that the CroqueMr fork gives
  this label, so that a skin made for either reads both);
- videodvoutput: how the Dolby Vision video goes out: native, hdr10 (rebuilt and
  sent as HDR10), sdr (rebuilt and mapped to SDR); empty otherwise;
- videodvreason: why it does not go out natively, as the code the Dolby Vision
  page turns into words;
- videodvlayers: the layers native output draws (FEL, MEL, BL, FELGAP, MELSKIP);
- videodvoutputchoice: the name of the output chosen for the video, where there
  is more than one to choose from.
The first four are what the window system publishes for the player information
every half second while it draws (PublishDVInfo()): one source, no new reading
of the hardware. hades.out.hdrtype is new there, taken from what Kodi gives the
output (native Dolby Vision, or the EOTF of SetHDR() with HDR10+ where its
metadata are queued or the rebuilt picture carries them), so that it is known
with the player information closed too (hades.out.signal, which reads the
connector back, is only there while the dialog is shown). On a platform without
the Dolby Vision bridge the labels are empty.

PlayerControl(HadesDVOutput) asks for the output of the video with the list
dialog of the skin, as the setting lists it, and applies the answer as the
setting does (the video stream opens again where it is). A list closed another
way, or the output already chosen, changes nothing. The list, its availability
and the way it is applied are one code with the video settings
(CGUIDialogVideoSettings::DVOutputChoices(), ApplyDVOutput()): what the setting
does is unchanged. A key of a keymap can be given that builtin.

The idea of the labels and of a quicker way to choose the output is from the
CroqueMr fork (Player.Process(...) labels, quick rendering selector) and from
YBLOD; written anew on what Hades publishes.
